// The column the text is laid out in: the window less its margins, but never
// so narrow that it cannot hold a word. `lay_wrap` breaks a line when the pen
// passes `w * 64`, so a width at or below zero breaks after every word and
// lays the document out one word to a line. A window can be dragged that
// narrow, so the floor is not hypothetical.
ed_lay_w(int w) {
  int lw = w - 40;
  if(lw < 40) {
    lw = 40;
  }
} return int lw;
(640):(600)
(80):(40)
(0):(40)
(10):(40)
(200):(160)
